title: adventurer_purpose
---
What drove you to pursue such a life?
-> To overcome adversaries and challenges #paneldetails=Gain_1_Proficiency_after_each_Elite_and_Boss_battles
	<<enable_elite_boss_proficiency>>
    You welcomed every challenge as an opportunity to prove yourself. The greater the obstacle, the greater the satisfaction of overcoming it.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To forge both your body and mind #paneldetails=Gain_5_Affinity
	<<change_affinity 5>>
    You sought to become someone who could endure anything the world threw at you. Through hardship, you would sharpen both body and mind into something stronger.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To discover uncharted horizons #paneldetails=Reduce_Light_drain_from_node_movement_by_50%
	<<set_light_loss 1>>
   The unknown called you. You longed to venture beyond familiar lands and see places no one had seen before
	<<jump reason>>
===

title: scholar_purpose
---
What drove you to pursue such a life?
-> To unravel the secrets of the world #paneldetails=Gain_1_Insight_at_the_start_of_each_act
	<<enable_insight_at_act_start>>
    You were captivated by the unknown. Every mystery left unanswered only stirred your curiosity further, driving you to seek truths hidden from ordinary men.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To harness arcanic might #paneldetails=Gain_1_Arcana
	<<change_arcana 1>>
    You saw magic as the greatest expression of knowledge. You wished to understand its nature, master its power, and reach heights no ordinary scholar could.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To illuminate others towards the path of Light #paneldetails=Gain_15_Light_at_the_start_of_each_act
	<<enable_light_at_act_start>>
   Knowledge, to you, was meant to be shared. You wished to guide others through their ignorance and help them find their own path toward the Light.
	<<jump reason>>

===

title: doctor_purpose
---
What drove you to pursue such a life?
-> To lend your hand to those in need #paneldetails=Gain_100_Vigor
	<<change_vigor 100>>
    You wished to be someone people could rely on in their darkest moments. To ease suffering, save lives, and give hope to those who had none.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To master the intricacies of human anatomy #paneldetails=Gain_1_Potency
	<<change_potency 1>>
    The human body fascinated you. You wanted a deep understanding of every bone, organ, and mechanism that allowed life to persist.
	<<jump reason>>
-> To amass vast wealth and renown #paneldetails=Gain_600_Gold_and_1_Insight
	<<change_gold 600>>
	<<change_insight 1>>
   You dreamed of becoming a renowned physician, not merely for the sake of helping others, but for the wealth and recognition that came with it.
	<<jump reason>>

===

title: reason
---
But you never did any of those things, because you…
-> Found other things to enjoy #paneldetails=Gain_1_Abundance_and_2_Capacity
	<<change_abundance 1>>
	<<change_capacity 2>>
    You kept finding things far more interesting, and in the end, that dream of yours became nothing more than a distant memory.
-> Were too afraid to take a single step #paneldetails=Remove_1_copy_of_Slash_and_Guard_from_the_starting_deck
	<<remove_initial_card Slash>>
	<<remove_initial_card Guard>>
    Paralyzed by the fear of failure and the uncertainty, you let every opportunity slip away untouched.
-> Had to stay with your family #paneldetails=Put_1_random_Uncommon_or_higher_card_into_your_deck
	<<add_random_uncommon_card>>
    Duty and affection binds you to your home, putting your own aspirations on hold to support the people you love, not that it matters now anyway…
<<jump resolution>>
